# Reference localization validation

These rules apply only to localization in retained `react/src/` reference source.
They do not define native localization ownership or build commands; use the
[reference entry](../../README.md) and [documentation index](../../../../docs/README.md)
to find current Rust/GPUI contracts.

- Translation text, locale switching and fallback do not need standalone unit
  tests or key-inventory fixtures.
- Business tests may mock translation, but their assertions must protect behavior,
  state or contracts rather than enumerate locale names and translation keys.
